| **A2: Broken Authentication** | No auth in place. Adding login routes w/out proper password hashing/storage will make it trivial to masquerade. | Use `passport`, store passwords with bcrypt, enforce rate limits on login. |
| **A3: Sensitive Data Exposure** | The `/users` route gives away email addresses and could leak more data. | Only return `id` and `name` after authentication, and encrypt data at rest. |
| **A4: XML External Entities (XXE)** | Not relevant right now (no XML parsing). | Still safe. |
